[0.013, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Why did signups drop in mid-June 2026?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 95s over 8 steps, 33,228 tokens, 20 observations gathered, 14 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Signups genuinely dropped by about 50% starting 2026-06-16/17 (from ~214/day to ~107/day), a shift confirmed statistically and sustained through the end of available data on 2026-06-29.  [posthog.event_trend abc94eae]\r\n  No cause was found in any connected system: GitHub shows no commits, PRs, or deployments to the product or marketing-site repos in the surrounding weeks, PostHog has no matching feature flag or annotation, and Slack has no message or recorded decision referencing the drop.  [github.commits 0545e17f, github.deployment_history 14037068, github.commits a8857c7f, posthog.feature_flags 3fd38237, posthog.annotations"]
[0.000, "o", " 2b3f4af9, slack.search_messages 39c57e0f, slack.search_messages 8d8df5ac, slack.search_messages f67a7149, slack.find_decision 5f0ce315]\r\n  The uniform silence across every connected source is itself notable and should be checked as a possible data-collection gap before concluding no cause exists, and the actual driver should be sought outside these tools (e.g. paid acquisition, an external partner, or infra changes not tracked in GitHub/PostHog/Slack).  [github.commits 0545e17f, slack.search_messages 39c57e0f]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Signups fell by ~50% starting 2026-06-16/17, sustained through month end  (high)\r\n    - Daily signup count (event 'user signed up') averaged ~214.5/day before 2026-06-16 and ~107/day after, a level shift of -50.1% that a permutation test distinguishes from noise (p=0.0435).  [posthog.event_trend abc94eae]\r\n    - The lower rate (roughly 93-109 signups/day) persisted through the end of available data on 2026-06"]
[0.000, "o", "-29, indicating a sustained step change rather than a brief dip.  [posthog.event_trend abc94eae]\r\n  No product, marketing, or engineering artifact in the connected systems coincides with or explains the shift  (low)\r\n    - acme/product had zero commits recorded between 2026-06-10 and any later date checked through 2026-06-25, and zero deployments to either the web-preview or web-live environment in this period.  [github.commits 0545e17f, github.deployment_history 14037068]\r\n    - No pull requests of any state exist for acme/product, and a feature search for 'signup' in that repository returned no results.  [github.recent_prs 9c1f39f3, github.find_feature 7150e133]\r\n    - acme/marketing-site also had zero commits between 2026-06-10 and 2026-06-20.  [github.commits a8857c7f]\r\n    - No PostHog feature flag matching 'signup' exists, and no annotation matching 'signup' was recorded on the signups metric.  [posthog.feature_flags 3fd38237, posthog.annotations 2b3f4af9]\r\n    - Slack search for 'signups drop', 'signup"]
[0.000, "o", " broken', 'signup', and 'onboarding' across June 2026 (and a decision search for topic 'signup') returned zero matching messages or decisions.  [slack.search_messages 39c57e0f, slack.search_messages a1778582, slack.search_messages 8d8df5ac, slack.search_messages f67a7149, slack.find_decision 5f0ce315]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▇▇▆▇▇██▇█▇▇▇▆█▇▇██▇█▇▇▇████▇▇▇▇▇▇▁▁▁▁▁▂▁▁▁▂▁▂▁|  93 → 230\r\n                        2026-05-15 … 2026-06-29\r\n\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] A code deploy or feature change to the product app around 2026-06-16 caused the signup drop.\r\n      No commits or deployments exist for acme/product in the entire surrounding window, which would rule this out directly -- but this null result is "]
[0.001, "o", "equally consistent with an instrumentation or connector gap as with a genuinely quiet repo, so it is treated as inconclusive rather than a hard contradiction.\r\n  [inconclusive] A marketing-site change (e.g. to the signup landing page or campaign) drove the drop.\r\n      No commits to acme/marketing-site appear in the window either, and no Slack discussion references any marketing or onboarding change; without a positive signal this cannot be confirmed or ruled out on direct evidence.\r\n  [contradicted] An internal team discussion or incident acknowledges the signup drop and names a cause.\r\n      Slack searches for 'signups drop', 'signup', and 'onboarding' in the relevant window, and a decision search for topic 'signup', all returned zero results, indicating no team conversation exists on record about this.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P1 Check the signup event's client/server instrumentation and any analytics SDK or tracking-plan change a"]
[0.000, "o", "round 2026-06-16-17 directly with the engineering team, since no repository, deployment, or Slack record in the connected tools captures a cause.\r\n      why: The magnitude and abruptness of the shift (a clean halving sustained for two weeks) is consistent with either a real demand-side event or an instrumentation change, and none of the connected systems (GitHub, PostHog, Slack) hold a record of either as of this investigation.\r\n      [posthog.event_trend abc94eae, posthog.list_events 0f19078e]\r\n  P2 Verify with the team whether any change outside the tools connected here (e.g. paid acquisition spend, an ad platform pause, a partner integration, or infra outside these three repos) occurred on or immediately before 2026-06-16.\r\n      why: All GitHub, PostHog, and Slack channels searched show no record of a cause, so the explanation likely lies outside this tenant's connected sources rather than being absent altogether.\r\n      [github.commits 0545e17f, slack.search_messages 39c57e0f]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n-----"]
[0.000, "o", "-------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Every explanatory source (GitHub commits/PRs/deployments for two repos, PostHog feature flags and annotations, Slack search and decisions) returned empty for the exact window of the drop. This pattern -- uniform silence across every connected system -- is at least as consistent with a connector or sync gap in this environment as with genuine inactivity, and cannot be distinguished from that here.\r\n  - The 'user signed up' event has no description or verified flag in the PostHog event catalog (unlike most other server-side events, which are marked verified:true), raising the possibility this event's instrumentation itself changed or is only partially reliable around the shift date.\r\n  - 4 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[1]: The searches only cover narrow keyword queries and limited date windo"]
[0.000, "o", "ws (e.g., marketing-site commits only checked 2026-06-10 to 06-20, Slack searches limited to specific terms lik\r\n- executive_summary[2]: Evidence only shows two empty queries (github commits, slack search) not PostHog, so 'every connected source' and the recommendation is a reasonable inference but overstates covera\r\n- findings[1].claims[0]: The evidence shows zero commits since 2026-06-10 (no end date specified) and zero deployments in an unspecified window, but nothing establishes the specific cutoff of 2026-06-25.\r\n- findings[1].claims[4]: The claim aggregates five zero-result searches accurately, though the 'signup' and 'onboarding' queries only covered partial June windows (6/14-6/20, 6/10-6/25) rather than all of \r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - GitHub commit, PR, and deployment queries for acme/product and acme/marketing-site returned zero rows for the entire window surrounding the drop (2026-05-15 through 2026-06-25), which is unusua"]
[0.000, "o", "l for active repositories and may indicate a connector gap rather than genuine inactivity.\r\n  - The 'user signed up' event lacks a description and verified flag, unlike other cataloged server-side events, so its instrumentation reliability could not be independently confirmed.\r\n  - 12 of the 14 cited observation(s) returned no results (github.commits, github.deployment_history, github.find_feature, github.recent_prs, posthog.annotations, posthog.feature_flags, slack.find_decision, slack.search_messages). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  0545e17f  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  a8857c7f  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  14037068  github.deployment_history  eval://github__deployment_history\r\n  7150e133  github.find_feature  eval://github__find_feature\r\n  9c1f39f3  github.recent_prs  eval://github__recent_prs\r\n  2b3f4af9  posthog.a"]
[0.000, "o", "nnotations  eval://posthog__annotations\r\n  abc94eae  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  3fd38237  posthog.feature_flags  eval://posthog__feature_flags\r\n  0f19078e  posthog.list_events  eval://posthog__list_events\r\n  5f0ce315  slack.find_decision  eval://slack__find_decision\r\n  39c57e0f  slack.search_messages  eval://slack__search_messages\r\n  a1778582  slack.search_messages  eval://slack__search_messages\r\n  8d8df5ac  slack.search_messages  eval://slack__search_messages\r\n  f67a7149  slack.search_messages  eval://slack__search_messages\r\n"]
